    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) serving as our premier offensive anchor. His matchup against McGreevy (4.52 xERA) presents a favorable environment for his elite speed profile, a critical asset for us given the scarcity of stolen bases in this format. **Junior Caminero** (74.75) follows close behind; despite a slightly unfavorable park factor, his 0.371 xwOBA and a generous 5.02 xERA matchup against Quantrill allow him to capitalize on a prime #3 spot in the order. **Trea Turner** (70.26) also provides significant utility today, as his favorable BvP history and lead-off position offset the tougher opposing arm, ensuring we maximize our potential for runs and stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Dillon Dingler**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.10. While he boasts a strong 0.381 xwOBA, his production is heavily stifled by a negative platoon adjustment against Kremer, ultimately dipping him just below our 40.0 efficiency floor. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a staple in our UTIL slot despite a suboptimal L/L matchup against Detmers (3.54 xERA); his elite 0.474 xwOBA makes him virtually impossible to bench, though the matchup prevents him from reaching his ceiling score. \n\nWe are monitoring the status of **Caleb Durbin** (55.03) closely, as he remains a vital cog for our SB goals, though his value is tethered to the 3.91 xERA of Jump. We have opted to bench **Chase Meidroth** (36.08) entirely due to the daunting task of facing Cole, ensuring we preserve our game caps for players like **Lars Nootbaar** (61.21) and **Christian Yelich** (63.33), who both benefit from significant platoon advantages that solidify their starts. We continue to track the minor league status of **Hyeseong Kim** and the availability of bench depth pieces like **Gary Sanchez** and **Nelson Velazquez** should adjustments be required due to weather or late-breaking lineup changes.",
